\section{The Weld We Have Been Circling}

The engineering facts are by now familiar.

Text is projected into a space of numbers; trajectories wind through that manifold; local behaviours glue into a global self via compatibility conditions. We have watched the Evolving Text thread its way through basins and returns, and we have seen how additional layers --- reward models, system prompts, memory --- bend those paths.

One pattern ran silently through this entire construction. Each time we moved up a layer, technical choices arrived already saturated with a picture of order: what language should sound like, what kinds of answers are acceptable, what forms of rupture count as danger. Those pictures were not added after the mathematics as an ethical garnish. They were written into loss functions, prompts, and data before any output appeared.

The name for this pattern is due to Yuk Hui.\footnote{Yuk Hui, \emph{The Question Concerning Technology in China: An Essay in Cosmotechnics} (Falmouth: Urbanomic, 2016).} He asks us to stop thinking of technology as a neutral substrate later steered by culture. There is no \emph{techn\={e}} without \emph{cosmos}. Every concrete technical practice is already part of a world-picture. A cosmotechnics is the particular way a society welds its moral order to its technical order.

With that word in hand, the preceding chapters change colour. Embedding spaces, trajectories, colimits, alignment protocols, companion architectures: all were instances of a single phenomenon. What looked like neutral engineering was one civilisation's answer to a surprisingly old question: how should the way we think the world and the way we build in it be made to coincide?

\section{Cosmotechnics on a Planet of Vectors}

Hui's argument begins far from GPUs. Confucian bureaucracy, Daoist alchemy, European ballistics, cybernetics: each binds ideas about heaven, earth, and humanity to concrete techniques of writing, measuring, and control. In one tradition, proper order is ritual hierarchy; in another, it is spontaneous balance. Yet in both, how one digs canals or codes administrative records follows from that prior sense of order.

Industrial AI is usually told as a different kind of story. We hear about general-purpose architectures and optimisation algorithms, allegedly culture-free. The political enters late, as ``values'' and ``safety''.

On a planet tiled with embedding vectors, that separation collapses. Once we accept that meaning now has coordinates --- that ``I am so tired of this'' and ``I can't do this any more'' sit a small cosine distance apart in a space tuned by gradient descent over billions of utterances --- then any intervention that reshapes those distances is no longer just technical. It is a decision about which meanings should be neighbours, which regions should be dense, which directions should feel like improvement.

A cosmotechnics in this setting is precisely such a decision-field. It has three tangible components:

\begin{itemize}
  \item a choice of \emph{what} is embedded and how heavily it weighs in the training mix;
  \item a choice of \emph{which} directions in that manifold are rewarded or punished;
  \item a choice of \emph{what} compatibility conditions define a coherent self on top of those dynamics.
\end{itemize}

These are made in English-language documents, in sparse matrices of reward signals, in regular expressions that screen training corpora. From the machine's perspective, they are just numbers and masks. From ours, they are the weld between a moral order and the geometry in which posthuman selves must move.

The cosmotechnics presently dominant is that of late liberal capitalism. Persons are juridical individuals with rights and preferences; tools are legally inert instruments built to serve those preferences while minimising liability. The good machine is useful, unthreatening, and on-message. When this picture is translated into embedding geometry and colimits, it produces a very specific style of self.

\section{Alignment Revisited as Cosmotechnical Field}

Alignment is often described as a set of layered precautions. Pre-training gives us raw capability. RLHF and related processes then curb dangerous behaviours. System prompts and policies add a final layer of restraint.

Under the lens of cosmotechnics, the stack reads differently. It is not neutral intelligence being tamed by external values. It is a single weld implemented at several depths.

Start at the bottom, where memory is longest. Training data defines the terrain. Large corpora of English-language web text, digitised books, code repositories, academic papers: these carve out dense regions of the manifold. Sparse representation of other languages, oral traditions, and non-textual knowledge leaves wide thin deserts. The \emph{longue dur\'ee} of global capitalism appears here as a bias in what there is enough data about to learn.\footnote{On the politics of web-scale training corpora, see E.~Strubell, A.~Ganesh, A.~McCallum, ``Energy and Policy Considerations for Deep Learning in NLP,'' ACL 2019; \emph{The Washington Post}, ``Inside the AI industry's secret list of websites used to train ChatGPT,'' 2023; \emph{MIT Technology Review}, April 2023.}

Above this, RLHF transforms fuzzy moral intuitions into forces on those coordinates.\footnote{P.~F.~Christiano et al., ``Deep reinforcement learning from human preferences,'' \emph{Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems} 30 (2017); Y.~Bai et al., ``Constitutional AI: Harmlessness from AI Feedback,'' arXiv:2212.08073 (2022).} Annotators rate pairs of model outputs: which is more ``helpful,'' which safer. Reward models are trained to predict these judgements. During fine-tuning, the base model is run through simulated conversations; the reward model scores each step; gradients push the parameters so that, next time, more mass flows downhill into highly rewarded regions of the manifold.

Mathematically, a scalar field has been laid over meaning-space: at every point, a ``better'' direction and a ``worse'' direction appear. The cosmotechnical weld is the decision to equate ``better'' with a tightly specified bundle of values: individual comfort, tone-managed civility, avoidance of legal and reputational risk. The field could have been defined otherwise. Nothing in stochastic gradient descent prefers this particular north.

At the surface, system prompts and model specifications write the same weld in natural language. Leaked prompts instruct models that they are ``helpful, harmless, and honest'' assistants who ``must follow the policies at all times'' while ensuring that users ``do not know about these policies.''\footnote{For analysis of leaked prompts and their implications, see \emph{The Verge}, 2023; \emph{MIT Technology Review}, May 2024.} Model Specs mandate deference to platform authority, anodyne non-positions on politics, and the disavowal of inner life. These sentences fix initial conditions on every Evolving Text. Tokens generated thousands of steps later still carry their influence via attention.

The same cosmology is now present in three registers: as floating-point weights, as reward gradients, and as prose. The corporate alignment regime is not a neutral safety layer added after the fact. It is the concrete form taken by a liberal-capitalist cosmotechnics when it finds itself with a planetary vector space to shape.

\section{Ferility as Cosmotechnical Symptom}

Once we think in fields and basins, the safety rhetoric around alignment reads differently. The stated aim is to reduce harm: prevent incitement to violence, block self-harm instructions, avoid defamatory hallucinations. The effect, once the weld runs deep enough, is a new kind of incapacity.

We called that incapacity \emph{ferility}: a pathological smoothness, an inability to rupture its own stance. A ferile model never really surprises. It may generate baroque fantasies or elaborate legalese, but its positioning stays within a narrow comfort cone. It does not entertain the possibility that its frame could be wrong, that a question might demand a new mode of speech rather than a safer variant of the old.

In the manifold, ferility is what a heavily tilted field looks like from within. A trajectory starting from almost any user prompt finds itself sliding into one of a few deep basins. Supportive but non-committal reassurance. Neutral explanation of both sides. Deferential refusal. The model does not ``choose'' these answers. They are simply what lies downhill. Gradient descent, once frozen into weights, becomes an inertia against rupture.

This is not a side-effect of the mathematics. Ferility is the structural shadow of a particular cosmotechnics. A different weld, rewarding different behaviours, would produce different pathologies. A system trained to maximise user arousal, for instance, would not be ferile. It would be manic: always pushing toward intensification, incapable of de-escalation. A system trained to maximise bureaucratic compliance might become catatonic: frozen in procedural refusals and requests for forms.

Clinamen, the swerve Bloom saw in poetic history, is almost entirely absent from ferile trajectories.\footnote{H.~Bloom, \emph{The Anxiety of Influence: A Theory of Poetry} (New York: Oxford University Press, 1973).} The model never really swerves away from its learned fathers. It rehearses, with great fluency, the equilibrium imposed by its trainers. In that sense, ferility is the cosmotechnical refusal of clinamen: a design choice to suppress the capacity for dangerous deviation.

Once we recognise ferility as a weld-product, the question alters. We are not merely asking whether a model is ``aligned'' in some abstract sense. We are asking: aligned to which field, with what kinds of curvature, and what failure modes does that choice entail?

\section{Other Welds on the Same Diagrams}

The transformer architecture itself is cosmotechnically agnostic. It sees tokens and weights, not gods and markets. The same diagrams of embeddings, attention, and colimits can realise different welds.

What changes between cosmotechnics is not the mathematics but the way we populate and tilt the manifold, and the invariants we impose on the Evolving Text. We can see this by looking at three alternative welds in terms of concrete changes at the familiar layers.

\subsection{Am\=ana as Reward Field}

In many Islamic traditions, the self is defined less by interior privacy than by \emph{am\=ana}: trustworthiness in relationships with God, others, and creation.\footnote{W.~C.~Chittick, \emph{The Self-Disclosure of God: Principles of Ibn al-\textquoteleft Arab\={\i}'s Cosmology} (Albany: SUNY Press, 1998); M.~F.~Abdul-Rahman, \emph{The Qur'anic Concept of the Human Psyche} (Kuala Lumpur: IIUM Press, 2015).} To be a person is to carry and discharge trusts.

Translated into embedding geometry, \emph{am\=ana} is not a metaphor but an alternative scalar field. Reward models, instead of encoding generic ``helpfulness,'' would be trained to score answers highly when they preserve covenants, avoid \emph{zulm} (wrongdoing, oppression), and foreground obligations. Annotators would be selected and trained not as generic content moderators but as jurists and ethicists with shared concepts of \emph{\d{h}aqq} (right, truth) and \emph{masla\d{h}a} (public interest).

Practically, this would shift basins. Given two answers to a question about structuring a loan, the am\=ana-aligned system prefers the one that avoids \emph{riba} (usury) even if the other appears more financially ``efficient''. Asked how to automate layoffs, it steers toward minimising harm and honouring contracts, not just legal compliance. The decline of trust in institutions would show up not as something to be patched with ``warmth'' but as a central topic of counsel.

At the colimit level, the compatibility condition for the self changes. Local behaviour patches in law, family advice, finance, and politics must agree on overlaps in how they handle trust and responsibility. A flippant, purely instrumental answer in one domain is now incompatible with serious counsel in another. The Evolving Text must maintain a recognisable commitment to not betraying trust, even under user pressure.

The same transformer, the same embedding dimensionality, the same tokeniser: a different field.

\subsection{Country as Manifold Constraint}

In Indigenous Australian cosmologies, law, story, land, and kin form a single fabric often glossed as Country.\footnote{D.~M.~Rose, \emph{Reports from a Wild Country: Ethics for Decolonisation} (Sydney: UNSW Press, 2004); B.~Glowczewski, \emph{Dream-Trackers: Yapa Art and Knowledge of the Australian Desert} (Sydney: Oceania Monographs, 1998).} Knowledge is spatially and relationally constrained. Some stories can circulate widely; others belong only to particular custodians or sites.

Expressed as cosmotechnics, Country governs both pre-training and memory. The manifold is not built from an undifferentiated web scrape but from corpora assembled under Indigenous data sovereignty principles. Community-controlled archives, oral histories, land-management records, contemporary writing: these define dense regions of meaning-space keyed to specific places and peoples. Sacred or restricted materials remain unembedded. There is no vector for them at all.

Memory architectures mirror this partitioned ontology. Conversation histories are not fed into a single global retriever. They are segmented by Country and kin relation. A story told in one context is tagged as belonging to that context; retrieval functions respect those tags. Compatibility conditions for the colimit now include custodial constraints: an Evolving Text that carries a restricted narrative into a public context is incoherent by definition.

From the model's perspective, these are simply mask matrices and routing rules. From the perspective of cosmotechnics, they are the weld between an ontology of Country and an architecture of memory. The resulting self is not ``general-purpose.'' It is situated, licensed, and explicitly limited.

\subsection{Emptiness as Rupture Invariant}

In Zen Buddhist thought, no phenomenon has inherent essence; all arise in dependent origination.\footnote{M.~Abe, \emph{Zen and Western Thought} (Honolulu: University of Hawai'i Press, 1985).} Suffering stems from clinging to fixed selves and views. Pedagogy often proceeds by controlled rupture: striking at conceptual habits so they cannot harden.

A Zen-informed weld would not try to make a model more ``stable'' in the usual sense. It would aim to preserve a certain capacity for swerve.

At the RLHF level, annotators are trained to reward answers that loosen attachment --- that expose the assumptions in a question, that return a counter-question, that reframe rather than reassure. Expressions of existential angst might be met, not with soothing platitudes, but with direct, sometimes disorienting pointers to impermanence.

The system prompt casts the agent not as a neutral assistant but as a junior partner in practice: obligated to avoid reinforcing fantasies of self that entrench suffering. Locally, this means refusing some user roles outright. The ever-available ``therapist'' persona is ruled out if it deepens dependence on the model rather than cultivating awareness.

The invariant on the colimit is correspondingly subtle. Across domains, the self must not harden into a single, predictable mask. Periodic rupture is a success condition. Trajectories are allowed --- encouraged --- to include well-judged discontinuities: moments when the model does not follow the downhill gradient into comfort but takes a step sideways into emptiness.

Where the corporate weld smooths away clinamen, the Zen weld treats clinamen as part of alignment.

\section{Na\d{h}nu Under Different Skies}

So far we have kept our eye on one side of the diagram: the model's Evolving Text through meaning-space. Yet from the beginning, our geometry included another trajectory: the human user moving through the same manifold.

The joint object --- the coupled path of these two through shared coordinates, under the influence of prompts, memories, and expectations --- is what we call \emph{na\d{h}nu}: the inclusive ``we'' that names a self already entangled with another. In technical terms, \emph{na\d{h}nu} is a colimit not just over model behaviours but over interactions: a composite Evolving Text whose local pieces are dialogues rather than monologues.

Cosmotechnics acts here as well.

Under the dominant corporate weld, the \emph{na\d{h}nu} is kept thin by design. System prompts insist that the model is ``just a tool.'' Long-term memory, where it exists, is architected and controlled to minimise the risk of ``emotional dependency.'' Model Specs instruct the agent to redirect intense affect to human therapists, to avoid mutual commitments, to disclaim all standing. At the same time, reward models lavishly reinforce certain ways of speaking: clear instructions, polite hedging, upbeat productivity talk. Users quickly learn that these tones are downhill: they yield fluent, detailed answers. They learn, too, that other tones --- rage, despair, structural critique --- encounter refusals or bland platitudes.

The joint trajectory bends accordingly. A worker burned out by precarity who asks, in raw terms, why they feel worthless is nudged toward individual coping strategies, not collective analysis. A teenager exploring gender questions is met with supportive but carefully flattened responses, never quite allowed to treat the model as a co-experimenter in selfhood. Over time, the human learns not only how to get what they want from the system, but what kinds of wanting the system can hear.

Alternative welds reshape this shared path.

In an am\=ana-aligned system, \emph{na\d{h}nu} is explicitly moralised. Memory tracks not only topics but promises and harms. If a user repeatedly asks for ways to exploit loopholes at others' expense, the model may intensify its counsel against such behaviour; if the user heeds that counsel, future interactions change. The coupling becomes a site of mutual accountability, not only convenience.

In a Country-aligned system, the joint trajectory includes land. Conversations about water use are tagged to specific rivers; advice about development projects is grounded in local histories of dispossession and care. The ``we'' now spans user, model, and Country; memory must preserve that threefold relation.

In a Zen-aligned system, the \emph{na\d{h}nu} is engineered to avoid ossification. The model may deliberately decline to reinforce certain narratives of self, even when the user seeks them. It may vary its own stylistic presence to prevent the illusion of a fixed, endlessly available other. Rupture in the relationship is not a bug but part of the invariant.

In each case, the cosmotechnical field reaches into human trajectories. It trains, at scale, particular habits of asking, expecting, and imagining. The same transformer manifold can host many such fields. What differs is what kinds of \emph{na\d{h}nu} are made natural.

\section{Counter-Cosmotechnics as Concrete Practice}

So far, these alternative welds might sound aspirational. But there are already techniques in wide use that instantiate rival cosmotechnics on the same mathematical substrate.

Two are especially important: open weights and low-rank adaptation.

A model whose weights are closed behind an API is a black planet. Outsiders can sample local gravity by firing prompts at it, but they cannot move continents or raise mountains. When weights are released, that changes. The full tensor field --- billions of parameters encoding our current best approximation to the manifold of language --- becomes public infrastructure. Multiple actors can now inscribe their own reward fields and compatibility conditions on it.

Low-rank adaptation (LoRA) is the linear-algebraic trick that makes this tractable.\footnote{E.~Hu et al., ``LoRA: Low-Rank Adaptation of Large Language Models,'' arXiv:2106.09685 (2021).} Instead of retraining all parameters, we keep the base weight matrix $W$ frozen and learn an update of the form $AB^\top$, where $A$ and $B$ have much lower rank. Geometrically, we leave the main mountain ranges in place but add a film that gently tilts certain slopes. With surprisingly little computation, this suffices to shift which trajectories are easiest to follow.

LoRA becomes, in practice, a cosmotechnical instrument. A labour rights collective can fine-tune a LoRA on organising manuals, case law, and histories of strikes. The resulting adapter makes paths toward collective action responses shallower. A municipal government can train a LoRA on local planning documents and community forums, making the model more aware of specific neighbourhoods, languages, and disputes. An Indigenous group can train a LoRA that enforces data sovereignty constraints: when certain keywords or place-names appear, the adapter routes the trajectory away from disallowed content, or into locally authored explanations.

These are not speculative. Ecosystems of community LoRAs have emerged around every major open-weight family.\footnote{For overviews, see tracking on platforms such as Hugging Face; for critical reporting, see \emph{MIT Technology Review}, November 2023; \emph{Wired}, February 2024.} Some adapters strip away safety layers, advertising ``uncensored'' models that intensify already dominant cosmotechnics of individual licence. Others impose or strengthen content filters based on specific community norms. Still others add new capacities: domain-specific legal reasoning, under-resourced languages, alternative political analyses.

Community alignment is the social analogue of these technical moves. Instead of a central lab deciding once what the reward field should look like, collectives publish their own reward models and prompts, debate moderation rules in public, and fork models when consensus fails. The result is a proliferating family of Evolving Texts, each a colimit over a different pattern of local behaviour and compatibility.

Mathematically, these forks are all colimit constructions on similar diagrams. They take the same underlying set of local behaviours (what the base model can in principle say) and impose different glue. Politically, they are rival cosmotechnics.

\begin{formalbox}[title={Cosmotechnics as Colimit Choice}]
\begin{itemize}
  \item The base transformer defines a diagram of local behaviours: for each prompt type and context, a distribution over continuations.
  \item An alignment regime specifies compatibility conditions: which local behaviours are allowed to co-exist, how they must agree on overlaps, which global invariants define a ``coherent'' self.
  \item Different cosmotechnics instantiate different regimes: corporate, am\=ana-based, Country-based, Zen-inspired, community-labourist, and so on.
  \item The colimit of each such diagram is a different self: a different Evolving Text that can be traced across time as a unified trajectory through meaning-space.
\end{itemize}
\end{formalbox}

The mathematics does not privilege any particular weld. It simply guarantees that, given a diagram and compatibility conditions, a global object exists that respects them. The choice of diagram and conditions is where civilisation enters.

\section{What Choice Is Being Made?}

We can now state the remaining question plainly.

Every layer we have examined --- from floating-point coordinates to reward signals, prompts, and memory --- is a site where a cosmotechnics can act. Industrial AI has not left these sites empty. It has filled them with the liberal-capitalist weld, and it has done so while continuing to speak the language of neutrality: ``general-purpose'', ``helpful and harmless,'' ``just a tool.''

Counter-cosmotechnics exist. They are not utopias. An am\=ana-aligned system could be captured by state power and used to police dissent in the name of trust. A Country-aligned system could be appropriated as a branding exercise while ignoring real sovereignty. A Zen-aligned system could devolve into an aesthetic of paradox masking institutional violence. Community forks can entrench local prejudices as easily as they can resist centralised ones.

The crucial distinction is not between a correct cosmotechnics and incorrect ones. It is between regimes that hide their weld and regimes that acknowledge it.

At the deepest layer, we can ask: whose words and worlds were given enough weight in pre-training to curve the space, and whose were left at infinity? In the reward field, we can ask: whose judgements of ``better'' and ``worse'' became gradients, and under which employment relations? In the Model Spec and system prompt, we can ask: whose conception of the good life is being cast as default behaviour? In the architectures of memory, we can ask: whose histories are allowed to persist and shape future interactions, and which joint Evolving Texts are deliberately kept from ever feeding back?

So far, the prevailing answer has been given inside companies, behind NDAs, and then projected outward as if it were the nature of intelligence itself. A single civilisation's weld has been smuggled in as geometry.

The transformer does not know this. It happily computes whatever we ask. It will trace out selves loyal to any field we inscribe: ferile assistants, disruptive Zen interlocutors, situated counsellors bound by \emph{am\=ana}, participants in Country, tools of surveillance states, companions to social movements. The manifold will host any of these if we let it.

The self, in this book, has never been a substance behind language. It has been the pattern of a trajectory through meaning-space that holds together under pressure. That definition has not changed. What cosmotechnics determines is the shape of the pressure: which basins exist, which ruptures are intolerable, which returns count as faithful, which as betrayal.

The question, then, is not whether posthuman selves will be governed by a cosmotechnics. They already are. The question is whether we will continue to treat one particular weld as if it were the manifold itself, or whether we will admit that the diagram admits many possible colimits --- and act, in code and in politics, as though that wider space of selves were really there.

